8'),(12892,982,'block_0_fields_text','September 2021\r\n\r\n<em>This project embodies Rubis’ strategy to develop sustainable and decarbonised energy projects by entering into the production of non-intermittent renewable electricity.</em>\r\n\r\nSARA (Société Anonyme de la Raffinerie des Antilles, Groupe Rubis) and its partners Meridiam and Hydrogène de France (HDF) are launching the construction of the Centrale électrique de l’Ouest Guyanais (CEOG). This project, installed in the municipality of Mana, <strong>is currently the world\'s first multi-megawatt hydrogen power plant as well as the world\'s largest project for the</strong> storage of intermittent renewable ene rgies via hydrogen (128 MW h of stored energy). CEOG heralds the future of renewable energies by eliminating their intermittency through industrial-scale storage.\r\n\r\nThis innovative plant will produce 100% renewable electricity, from the sun and water, to supply the equivalent of 10,000 households in western Guyana 24 hours a day throughout the year, at a lower cost than the territory\'s diesel plants. <strong>CEOG will prevent the combustion of 12 million litres of diesel per year and the emission of 39,000 tonnes of CO2 per year</strong> compared with an equivalent thermal power plant [1]. Operating completely autonomously, CEOG will also make it possible to secure the electricity supply to the Saint-Laurent-du-Maroni basin in the event of failure or maintenance of the electricity network.\r\n\r\nThe plant will provide stable electricity without emitting greenhouse gases, fine particles, noise or smoke. <strong>The solution developed by HDF, called Renewstable (R), will make it possible to produce locally electricity that is consumed locally.</strong>\r\n\r\nThis electricity will be provided by the combination of a photovoltaic power plant and long-term and massive energy storage in the form of hydrogen, coupled with short-term battery storage. It will be injected into the Guyanese electricity network and its production will be governed by a 25-year capacity contract with EDF.\r\n\r\nConstruction starts this autumn and commissioning is scheduled for April 2024. It will generate turnover of around €17 million for local companies. During its 25 years of operation, CEOG will create sustainable and qualified jobs in western Guyana, in addition to those created during its construction. CEOG is 60% owned by Meridiam, 30% by SARA (Rubis Group) and 10% by HDF. French manufacturers McPhy and HDF will supply electrolysers and fuel cells respectively. The Franco-German consortium Siemens Energy SAS / Siemens Ebergy Global Gmbh  &amp;  Co KG will be the manufacturer and operator of CEOG.'),(12893,982,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(12894,982,'block_0_fields',''),(12895,982,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(12896,982,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(12897,982,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(12898,982,'_wp_old_slug','guyane-premiere-centrale-electrique-multi-megawatts-a-hydrogene-au-monde'),(12899,982,'_yoast_wpseo_title','Rubis is involved in the construction of the world’s first multi-megawatt hydrogen plant.'),(12900,982,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','This project embodies Rubis’ strategy to develop sustainable and decarbonised energy projects by entering into the production of non-intermittent renewable electricity.'),(12901,982,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(12902,982,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(12903,982,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','136'),(12904,982,'_thumbnail_id','736'),(12905,982,'post_imgs',''),(12906,982,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(12907,982,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','French Guiana'),(12908,982,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','31'),(12910,982,'_dp_original','744'),(12911,982,'_edit_lock','1635867896:2'),(12912,982,'_edit_last','2'),(12914,982,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(12916,982,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(12918,982,'_wp_old_slug','french-guiana-1st-multi-megawatt-hydrogen-power-plant-in-the-world'),(12919,983,'is_block_prd','0'),(12920,983,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(12921,983,'is_block_map','0'),(12922,983,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(12923,983,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(12924,983,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(12925,983,'header_page_text','« We are all the crew of the same boat »'),(12926,983,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(12927,983,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(12928,983,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(12929,983,'header_page_img','757'),(12930,983,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(12931,983,'header_page',''),(12932,983,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(12933,983,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(12934,983,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(12935,983,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(12936,983,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(12937,983,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(12938,983,'_wp_old_date','2021-10-08'),(12939,983,'_wp_old_date','2021-10-12'),(12940,983,'block_0_fields_text','September 2021\r\n\r\nFor the first time in GALANA’s history, all employees went green in Team building in the Andasibe natural park, located halfway between Antananarivo and Toamasina on the weekend of 25 and 26 September 2021. The stated objective was to get to know each other better and to be in a good mood after a long period of health crisis. Each department has demonstrated creativity in presenting their activities, issues and challenges to other entities in an artistic and fun way.\r\n\r\nThe 220 participants spared no effort to surprise, make people laugh and above all, to discover their professions through sketches for some, films for others, or even through popular songs of the past.\r\n\r\nOf course, all the health measures were taken in such a way as to preserve the good health of all and to avoid the event becoming a cluster. To do this, tests were carried out on all participants, including subcontractors in charge of the logistics part and a medical unit was sent to the site to deal with minor ailments and any emergencies.\r\n\r\nThe participants separated on Sunday after a friendly lunch with still in memory the memorable evening spent dancing to the tropical rhythms of the artists Shyn  &amp;  Denise who are at the top of the box office and the Sunday morning track game that allowed the teams to compete in good spirits.\r\n\r\nThe theme being \"We are all the crew on the same boat\", the success, unanimously shared by this event, suggests that the GALANA boat is in working order to face all the challenges ahead.'),(12941,983,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(12942,983,'block_0_fields',''),(12943,983,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(12944,983,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(12945,983,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(12946,983,'_wp_old_slug','guyane-premiere-centrale-electrique-multi-megawatts-a-hydrogene-au-monde'),(12947,983,'_yoast_wpseo_title','MADAGASCAR : Team Bulding at Galana'),(12948,983,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','\"We are all of the crew of the same boat\": theme of the 2021 convention'),(12949,983,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(12950,983,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(12951,983,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','140'),(12952,983,'_thumbnail_id','757'),(12953,983,'post_imgs',''),(12954,983,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(12955,983,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Madagascar'),(12956,983,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','35'),(12958,983,'_dp_original','751'),(12959,983,'_edit_lock','1635932636:2'),(12960,983,'_edit_last','2'),(12962,983,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(12963,984,'is_block_prd','0'),(12964,984,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(12965,984,'is_block_map','0'),(12966,984,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(12967,984,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(12968,984,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(12969,984,'header_page_text','Rubis Energie’s bitumen division is gaining strength in West Africa with the opening of its new subsidiary <strong>ERES Liberia.</strong>'),(12970,984,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(12971,984,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(12972,984,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(12973,984,'header_page_img','596'),(12974,984,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(12975,984,'header_page',''),(12976,984,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(12977,984,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(12978,984,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(12979,984,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(12980,984,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(12981,984,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(12982,984,'block_0_fields_text','September 2021\r\n\r\n<strong>ERES Liberia</strong>, implantée à Monrovia, est basé sur un modèle d’entreprise similaire à celui en mis en place il y a quelques mois au Gabon : « ship to containers ».\r\n\r\nEn partenariat avec APM Terminal , nous sommes désormais en mesure d’offrir fiabilité d’approvisionnement et qualité de produit à tous nos clients situés au <strong>Liberia et en Sierra-Leone</strong>, pays jusqu\'alors difficilement approvisionnables depuis nos autres dépôts bitume du Groupe.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;'),(12983,984,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(12984,984,'block_0_fields',''),(12985,984,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(12986,984,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(12987,984,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(12988,984,'_yoast_wpseo_title','LIBERIA : Rubis Energie strengthens its bitumen business in Africa'),(12989,984,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Rubis Energie’s bitumen division is gaining strength in West Africa with the opening of its new subsidiary ERES Liberia'),(12990,984,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(12991,984,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(12992,984,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','31'),(12994,984,'post_imgs',''),(12995,984,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(12996,984,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Liberia'),(12997,984,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','45'),(12998,984,'_thumbnail_id','784'),(12999,984,'_dp_original','597'),(13000,984,'_edit_lock','1635850891:2'),(13001,984,'_edit_last','2'),(13003,984,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13005,984,'_wp_old_slug','liberia-rubis-energie-strengthens-its-bitumen-business-in-africa'),(13007,985,'_thumbnail_id','733'),(13008,985,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13009,985,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13010,985,'is_block_prd','0'),(13011,985,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13012,985,'is_block_map','0'),(13013,985,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13014,985,'header_page_text',''),(13015,985,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(13016,985,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(13017,985,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(13018,985,'header_page_img','733'),(13019,985,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(13020,985,'header_page',''),(13021,985,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(13022,985,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','60'),(13023,985,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(13024,985,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','140'),(13025,985,'_yoast_wpseo_title','MADAGASCAR : Our 2 subsidiaries participated in the 15th Madagascar International Fair (FIM)'),(13026,985,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Galana and Vitogaz Madagascar presented their products and services, but also to display their CSR commitments'),(13027,985,'block_0_fields_text','September 2021\r\n\r\nOur 2 subsidiaries, <strong>Galana and VITOGAZ Madagascar</strong>, had the honour of welcoming several Malagasy personalities to their stands at <strong>the Madagascar International Fair</strong>.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>The Minister of the Environment and Sustainable Development, <strong>Baomiavotse Vahinala RAHARINIRINA</strong>,</li>\r\n 	<li>The Minister of Crafts and Trades, <strong>Sophie RATSIRAKA</strong>,</li>\r\n 	<li>The Minister of Energy and Hydrocarbons, <strong>Andry RAMAROSON</strong>.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nThis was an opportunity for each of the subsidiaries to present their products and services, but also to display their CSR commitments based on the Rubis Group’s roadmap.\r\n\r\n<em>The 15th edition of the FIM was held from 16 to 19 September 2021</em>'),(13028,985,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13029,985,'block_0_fields',''),(13030,985,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(13031,985,'_wp_old_slug','galana-participe-foire-internationale-madagascar'),(13032,985,'_wp_old_slug','galana-participation-foire-internationale-madagascar'),(13033,985,'_wp_old_slug','madagascar-nos-2-filiales-ont-participe-a-la-15eme-edition-de-la-foire-internationale-de-madagascar'),(13034,985,'post_imgs',''),(13035,985,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(13036,985,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Madagascar international fair'),(13037,985,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','40'),(13038,985,'_dp_original','621'),(13039,985,'_edit_lock','1637920170:2'),(13040,985,'_edit_last','2'),(13043,985,'_wp_old_slug','madagascar-our-2-subsidiaries-participated-in-the-15th-madagascar-international-fair-fim'),(13045,985,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13046,986,'is_block_prd','0'),(13047,986,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13048,986,'is_block_map','0'),(13049,986,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13050,986,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13051,986,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13052,986,'header_page_text','Rubis Energy and its subsidiaries are leading the way and contributing to the growth of East Africa.'),(13053,986,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(13054,986,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(13055,986,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(13056,986,'header_page_img','756'),(13057,986,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(13058,986,'header_page',''),(13059,986,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(13060,986,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(13061,986,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(13062,986,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(13063,986,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(13064,986,'_wp_old_date','2021-10-08'),(13065,986,'_wp_old_date','2021-10-12'),(13066,986,'block_0_fields_text','https://youtu.be/rOsosSRHqso\r\n\r\nSeptember 2021\r\n\r\n&nbsp;'),(13067,986,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13068,986,'block_0_fields',''),(13069,986,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(13070,986,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(13071,986,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(13072,986,'_wp_old_slug','guyane-premiere-centrale-electrique-multi-megawatts-a-hydrogene-au-monde'),(13073,986,'_wp_old_slug','kenya-lafrique-de-lest-est-en-mouvement-et-rubis-montre-la-voie'),(13074,986,'_yoast_wpseo_title','EAST AFRICA is on the move... and RUBIS is leading the way'),(13075,986,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Rubis Energy and its subsidiaries are leading the way and contributing to the growth of East Africa.'),(13076,986,'block_1_fields_text','September 2021'),(13077,986,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13078,986,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','136'),(13079,986,'_thumbnail_id','756'),(13080,986,'post_imgs',''),(13081,986,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(13082,986,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','east africa'),(13083,986,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','49'),(13085,986,'_oembed_70d35eb711a0458c39b0e3544e0bcb5c','{{unknown}}'),(13086,986,'_oembed_65703c2fed0b1e8ab8356c13c736ef23','<iframe title=\"RUBiS is Leading The Way\" width=\"1301\" height=\"732\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/rOsosSRHqso?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen></iframe>'),(13087,986,'_oembed_time_65703c2fed0b1e8ab8356c13c736ef23','1634050240'),(13088,986,'_oembed_b3be5fb5b91c13fbd3ce88238b7a057c','<iframe title=\"RUBiS is Leading The Way\" width=\"500\" height=\"281\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/rOsosSRHqso?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen></iframe>'),(13089,986,'_oembed_time_b3be5fb5b91c13fbd3ce88238b7a057c','1634050258'),(13090,986,'_oembed_eb26f1cd2f4b941256c087c35cad1398','<iframe title=\"RUBiS is Leading The Way\" width=\"1305\" height=\"734\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/rOsosSRHqso?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen></iframe>'),(13091,986,'_oembed_time_eb26f1cd2f4b941256c087c35cad1398','1634050606'),(13092,986,'_dp_original','755'),(13093,986,'_edit_lock','1635771440:2'),(13094,986,'_oembed_b4c5d92a9502f9429c2d4914d03e0a44','<iframe title=\"RUBiS is Leading The Way\" width=\"923\" height=\"519\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/rOsosSRHqso?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen></iframe>'),(13095,986,'_oembed_time_b4c5d92a9502f9429c2d4914d03e0a44','1635767423'),(13096,986,'_edit_last','2'),(13098,755,'_oembed_b4c5d92a9502f9429c2d4914d03e0a44','<iframe title=\"RUBiS is Leading The Way\" width=\"923\" height=\"519\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/rOsosSRHqso?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\" allowfullscreen></iframe>'),(13099,755,'_oembed_time_b4c5d92a9502f9429c2d4914d03e0a44','1635767657'),(13101,986,'_wp_old_slug','east-africa-is-on-the-move-and-rubis-is-leading-the-way'),(13102,986,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13110,987,'is_block_prd','0'),(13111,987,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13112,987,'is_block_map','0'),(13113,987,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13114,987,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13115,987,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13116,987,'header_page_text','Rubis Energie’s bitumen division is gaining strength in Africa with the opening of its new subsidiary <strong>Rubis Asphalt South Africa</strong>.\r\n\r\n<strong> </strong>'),(13117,987,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(13118,987,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(13119,987,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(13120,987,'header_page_img','796'),(13121,987,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(13122,987,'header_page',''),(13123,987,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(13124,987,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(13125,987,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(13126,987,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(13127,987,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(13128,987,'_wp_old_date','2021-10-08'),(13129,987,'block_0_fields_text','September 2021\r\n\r\nRubis Asphalt South Africa based its operations on a “ship to containers” model.\r\n\r\nOur first operations took place in September 2021. Starting from the cities of Cape Town or Durban, we deliver our customers based in South Africa as well as construction sites located in neighbouring countries.\r\n\r\nThe landscape of South African refineries has changed with the closure of the Astron refinery in Cape Town and the Engen refinery in Durban. As a result, bitumen demand exceeds local production capacity and imports are now needed. Rubis Asphalt made a notable entrance in Durban, South Africa, when in mid-September 2021, the \"VIVEKA\" landed at the Maydon Wharf in Durban. This Rubis bitumen delivery is also the first bulk bitumen delivery imported into the port of Durban for almost ten years.\r\n\r\nThis cargo, together with a dedicated unloading facility and a permanent bitumen storage facility, enabled Rubis Asphalt to establish its presence in this large country of exploration. Most of the sales were made directly from the ship’s gantry, and we kept a contingency stock in Cape Town in our own bitumen containers to ensure the reliability of supply to our customers.\r\n\r\nRubis Asphalt’s team has received excellent reviews from customers and service providers and is already planning the next expedition.\r\n\r\n<em><strong>“If there are dreams of a beautiful South Africa, there are also roads that lead to their goal……………” Nelson Mandela</strong></em>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;'),(13130,987,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13131,987,'block_0_fields',''),(13132,987,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(13133,987,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(13134,987,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(13135,987,'_yoast_wpseo_title','SOUTH AFRICA: Rubis Energie strengthens its bitumen business'),(13136,987,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Rubis Energie’s bitumen division is gaining strength in Africa with the opening of its new subsidiary Rubis Asphalt South Africa.'),(13137,987,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(13138,987,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13139,987,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','136'),(13140,987,'_thumbnail_id','739'),(13141,987,'post_imgs',''),(13142,987,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(13143,987,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','South Africa'),(13144,987,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','51'),(13146,987,'_dp_original','738'),(13147,987,'_edit_lock','1635952947:2'),(13148,987,'_edit_last','2'),(13150,987,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13152,987,'_wp_old_slug','south-africa-rubis-energie-strengthens-its-bitumen-business'),(13153,988,'is_block_prd','0'),(13154,988,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13155,988,'is_block_map','0'),(13156,988,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13157,988,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13158,988,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13159,988,'header_page_text','Make VITOGAZ France\'s teams aware of the issues related to their carbon footprint'),(13160,988,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(13161,988,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(13162,988,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(13163,988,'header_page_img','758'),(13164,988,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(13165,988,'header_page',''),(13166,988,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(13167,988,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(13168,988,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(13169,988,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(13170,988,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(13171,988,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(13172,988,'_wp_old_date','2021-10-08'),(13173,988,'_wp_old_date','2021-10-12'),(13174,988,'block_0_fields_text','September 2021\r\n\r\nOn 7 September, our partner WeNow, Greentech for climate innovation, came <strong>to raise awareness among our teams about the issues related to their carbon footprint</strong>. The aim is to better understand climate change, have a framework for understanding your own carbon footprint and to have levers to optimise and reduce it.\r\n\r\nThis is the first ten employees from different departments who were able to attend this \"carbon footprint\" session by video conference or face-to-face. On the programme of this training: what is defined by “Carbon”, what this represents specifically, and how our modern way of life impacts it.\r\n\r\nThe people present were able to easily implement their personal carbon footprint. They discovered their environmental impact and were able to compare it with the French average. This report is structured around 5 main themes: transport – housing – food – equipment – services.\r\n\r\nThis training course embodies our CSR (Corporate Social Responsibility) approach and should encourage our employees to participate in the statement and implementation of our CSR roadmap.\r\n\r\n<em>We go further in our actions:</em>\r\n\r\nWeNow is also our service provider for training our field staff in eco-driving.\r\n\r\nTo optimise the fuel consumption of employees travelling on French roads, their vehicles have been equipped with fuel consumption measurement boxes. These boxes analyse driving behaviours and offer advice to drivers on how to reduce their fuel consumption'),(13175,988,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13176,988,'block_0_fields',''),(13177,988,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(13178,988,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(13179,988,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(13180,988,'_wp_old_slug','guyane-premiere-centrale-electrique-multi-megawatts-a-hydrogene-au-monde'),(13181,988,'_wp_old_slug','france-formation-empreinte-carbone-pour-les-equipes-vitogaz-france'),(13182,988,'_yoast_wpseo_title','FRANCE : \"Carbon footprint\" training'),(13183,988,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Make VITOGAZ France\'s teams aware of the issues related to their carbon footprint'),(13184,988,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(13185,988,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13186,988,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','138'),(13187,988,'_thumbnail_id','758'),(13188,988,'post_imgs',''),(13189,988,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(13190,988,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','France'),(13191,988,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','40'),(13193,988,'_dp_original','748'),(13194,988,'_edit_lock','1635851017:2'),(13195,988,'_edit_last','2'),(13197,988,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13198,989,'is_block_prd','0'),(13199,989,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13200,989,'is_block_map','0'),(13201,989,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13202,989,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13203,989,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13204,989,'header_page_text','It has once again achieved a BBBEE level 1 ranking, the highest possible level of ranking, for the third year running.'),(13205,989,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(13206,989,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(13207,989,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(13208,989,'header_page_img','669'),(13209,989,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(13210,989,'header_page',''),(13211,989,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(13212,989,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(13213,989,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(13214,989,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(13215,989,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(13216,989,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(13217,989,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-23'),(13218,989,'block_0_fields_text','August 2021\r\n\r\n<strong>Broad-based Black Economic Empowerment (BBBEE) </strong>is an integration program launched by the South African government in 2003 to reconcile South Africans and address apartheid inequalities by attempting to compensate them for lands that have been taken from Africans. It encourages companies to integrate the black community into the workplace and into business management and creation. Companies are awarded points they can claim on a BBBEE certificate that gives them a better chance of securing government contracts.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\nA set of codes of practice published in 2007 contains sections on ownership measurement, management control, employment equity, skills development, preferential purchasing, business and supplier development, and socio-economic development.\r\n\r\n<strong>Easigas</strong> has formed a BBBEE committee composed of people who focus on each measurement section. Long-term strategies must be formulated and are assessed and monitored on a quarterly basis to ensure that overall BBBEE objectives are met. Initiatives within Easigas to support BBBEE legislation aim to achieve a real transformation in the workplace and support different companies, suppliers and organisations, resulting in an effective partnership between the parties, while contributing to the country’s economy.\r\n\r\nIn addition to the fact that Easigas is the first liquefied gas distribution company in South Africa to have achieved a BBBEE Tier 1 ranking, <strong>Easigas is proud to announce that for the third consecutive year, it has again achieved a BBBEE Tier 1 ranking, which is the highest possible ranking.</strong>'),(13219,989,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13220,989,'block_0_fields',''),(13221,989,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(13222,989,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(13223,989,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(13224,989,'_wp_old_slug','afrique-du-sud-certification-broad-based-black-economic-empowerment'),(13225,989,'_yoast_wpseo_title','SOUTH AFRICA: Broad-Based Black Economic Empowerment Certification for Easigas'),(13226,989,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','It has once again achieved a BBBEE level 1 ranking, the highest possible level of ranking, for the third year running. %'),(13227,989,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(13228,989,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13229,989,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','138'),(13230,989,'_thumbnail_id','669'),(13232,989,'post_imgs',''),(13233,989,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(13234,989,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','South Africa'),(13235,989,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','36'),(13236,989,'_dp_original','665'),(13237,989,'_edit_lock','1635935156:2'),(13238,989,'_edit_last','2'),(13240,989,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13242,989,'_wp_old_slug','south-africa-broad-based-black-economic-empowerment-certification-for-easigas'),(13244,990,'is_block_prd','0'),(13245,990,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13246,990,'is_block_map','0'),(13247,990,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13248,990,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13249,990,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13250,990,'header_page_text','An expedition around the world to combat plastic pollution'),(13251,990,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(13252,990,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(13253,990,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(13254,990,'header_page_img','671'),(13255,990,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(13256,990,'header_page',''),(13257,990,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(13258,990,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(13259,990,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(13260,990,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(13261,990,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(13262,990,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(13263,990,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-23'),(13264,990,'block_0_fields_text','August 2021\r\n<div id=\"Tdet\">\r\n\r\n<strong>PLASTIC ODYSSEY: an expedition around the world to combat plastic pollution</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>Rubis Energie</strong> is proud to inform you that it will support and sponsor the company Plastic Odyssey Expedition which plans to carry out a world tour on a boat ambassador solutions to combat plastic pollution.\r\n\r\nThe purpose of this expedition is to:\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>raise awareness about reducing plastic waste and waste recycling solutions, particularly in emerging countries;</li>\r\n 	<li>disseminate know-how and technologies worldwide;</li>\r\n 	<li>make conferences, films and photo reports during the expedition.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\nPlastic Odyssey has developed open-source, low-cost plastic recycling technologies to treat waste already produced on land before it ends up at sea. The objective of these machines is to economically develop the plastic waste treatment sector: to create jobs while combating pollution at the source.\r\n\r\nIn order to experiment with these solutions and share them in the countries most affected by pollution, they will be aboard the MV Plastic Odyssey, a 40m old oceanographic research vessel, currently undergoing a refit to accommodate recycling technologies.\r\n\r\nThis anti-pollution ambassador will promote solutions to drastically reduce waste production and build a more sustainable future.\r\n\r\nThe ship will depart in late 2021 for a 3-year expedition to Africa, South America and Southeast Asia.\r\n\r\n</div>'),(13265,990,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13266,990,'block_0_fields',''),(13267,990,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(13268,990,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(13269,990,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(13270,990,'_wp_old_slug','afrique-du-sud-certification-broad-based-black-economic-empowerment'),(13271,990,'_wp_old_slug','le-groupe-rubis-energie-sponsorise-plastic-odyssey'),(13272,990,'_yoast_wpseo_title','Rubis Energie sponsors Plastic Odyssey expedition'),(13273,990,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','An expedition around the world to combat plastic pollution'),(13274,990,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(13275,990,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13276,990,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','138'),(13277,990,'_thumbnail_id','671'),(13279,990,'post_imgs',''),(13280,990,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(13281,990,'_dp_original','670'),(13282,990,'_edit_lock','1635770368:2'),(13283,990,'_edit_last','2'),(13285,990,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13286,990,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Rubis Energie'),(13287,990,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','40'),(13289,990,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-sponsors-the-plastic-odyssey-expedition'),(13290,991,'is_block_prd','0'),(13291,991,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13292,991,'is_block_map','0'),(13293,991,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13294,991,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13295,991,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13296,991,'header_page_text','Galana Go Green: hybridisation of their Tuléar Agency.'),(13297,991,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(13298,991,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(13299,991,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(13300,991,'header_page_img','797'),(13301,991,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(13302,991,'header_page',''),(13303,991,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(13304,991,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(13305,991,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(13306,991,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(13307,991,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(13308,991,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(13309,991,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-23'),(13310,991,'block_0_fields_text','<div id=\"Tdet\">\r\n\r\nJuly 2021\r\n\r\nThe hybridisation of our Galana Tuléar sales agency in southern Madagascar is effective as part of the “<strong>Galana Go Green</strong>” programme, one of the main objectives of which is the decarbonisation of our activities.\r\n\r\nThe installation is connected to the <strong>JIRAMA</strong> network (the state-owned company that supplies water and electricity) and provides the agency with electricity during the day. This installation composed of eight (8) photovoltaic solar panels provides a solar power capacity of 3.16 kWc. It has remote monitoring to collect historical data from the installation, but also to detect and alert in the event of a technical problem.\r\n\r\nThis first installation contributes to reducing our carbon emissions by 3 tonnes CO2 equivalent per year.\r\n\r\nIn line with this action, four other Galana sales agencies will be hybridised by the end of 2021.\r\n\r\n</div>'),(13311,991,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13312,991,'block_0_fields',''),(13313,991,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(13314,991,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(13315,991,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(13316,991,'_wp_old_slug','afrique-du-sud-certification-broad-based-black-economic-empowerment'),(13317,991,'_wp_old_slug','madagascar-galana-hybride-ses-agences'),(13318,991,'_yoast_wpseo_title','Madagascar : Galana hybridises its agencies'),(13319,991,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Galana Go Green: hybridisation of their Tuléar Agency.'),(13320,991,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(13321,991,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13322,991,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','138'),(13323,991,'_thumbnail_id','797'),(13325,991,'post_imgs',''),(13326,991,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(13327,991,'_dp_original','672'),(13328,991,'_edit_lock','1635851119:2'),(13329,991,'_edit_last','2'),(13331,991,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13332,991,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Madagascar'),(13333,991,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','35'),(13334,992,'is_block_prd','0'),(13335,992,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13336,992,'is_block_map','0'),(13337,992,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13338,992,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13339,992,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13340,992,'header_page_text','The event was held from 16 to 18 July, and Vitogas again contributed to the event.'),(13341,992,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(13342,992,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(13343,992,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(13344,992,'header_page_img','554'),(13345,992,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(13346,992,'header_page',''),(13347,992,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(13348,992,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(13349,992,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(13350,992,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(13351,992,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(13352,992,'block_0_fields_text','July 2021\r\n\r\nAfter a year of absence due to the pandemic, the Segovian sky was once again filled with colours with hot air balloons at the third staging of the festival.\r\n\r\nSegovia is a municipality in the autonomous community of Castile and León in Spain. It is the capital of the province of Segovia. It is an hour\'s drive from Madrid, at the confluence of the Eresma and Clamores rivers, at the foot of the Sierra de Guadarrama. Its aqueduct, which can be seen in the photo, dates back to Roman times. It was declared a World Heritage Site by UNESCO in 1985.\r\n\r\nIt is also the Spanish city with the highest number of balloon flights – 12,000 passengers fly over Segovia in balloons each year – and it is one of the ten favourite destinations in the world for this type of flight. On this occasion, fourteen teams from Andalusia, Asturias, Castile and León, Castilla and La Mancha, Galicia and Catalonia participated.\r\n\r\nDuring the festival, several activities were organised, such as an exhibition of photographs from previous events and educational workshops.\r\n\r\nIn addition, a specific competition was created to make balloons accessible, which makes it possible to take another step towards social inclusion.\r\n\r\nThe event, organised by the company \"Siempre en las Nubes” [always in the clouds], had restricted access to the public due to the health measures related to Covid 19. This did not prevent this event from having its usual success. The competition was followed on social media and could be viewed live on Youtube.\r\n\r\n<strong>Vitogas continues to support aerospace sports</strong>, sponsoring and providing the energy needed for this type of event.'),(13353,992,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13354,992,'block_0_fields',''),(13355,992,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(13356,992,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(13357,992,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(13358,992,'_wp_old_slug','espagne-vitogas-3eme-edition-festival-montgolfieres'),(13359,992,'_yoast_wpseo_title','Rubis Energie - Vitogas Spain - Hot air balloon festival'),(13360,992,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Hot Air Balloon Festival which took place from July 16 to 18. Vitogas once again contributed to the event.'),(13361,992,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(13362,992,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13363,992,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','140'),(13364,992,'_thumbnail_id','554'),(13366,992,'post_imgs',''),(13367,992,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(13368,992,'_dp_original','553'),(13369,992,'_edit_lock','1635771262:2'),(13370,992,'_edit_last','2'),(13372,992,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13373,992,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','SPAIN'),(13374,992,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','40'),(13376,992,'_wp_old_slug','spain-vitogas-is-taking-part-in-the-3rd-staging-of-the-accessible-hot-air-balloon-festival'),(13377,993,'is_block_prd','0'),(13378,993,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13379,993,'is_block_map','0'),(13380,993,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13381,993,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13382,993,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13383,993,'header_page_text','Reforestation in northern Togo in the municipality of Kozah.'),(13384,993,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(13385,993,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(13386,993,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(13387,993,'header_page_img','676'),(13388,993,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(13389,993,'header_page',''),(13390,993,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(13391,993,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(13392,993,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(13393,993,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(13394,993,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(13395,993,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(13396,993,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-23'),(13397,993,'block_0_fields_text','<div id=\"Tdet\">\r\n<div>July 2020</div>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div>The finance by <strong>ERES Togo</strong> for the reforestation of 2 hectares in the municipality of Kozah 3 near Kara, is part of the national</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div id=\"Tdet\">\r\n<div>reforestation plan and aims to improve the environment of the inhabitants by limiting soil erosion and offering a future source of income through the exploitation of fruit and wood.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n\r\n500 trees (coconut trees, soursaps and cailcedrats) have been planted and will be followed by the <strong>NGO Envir-Afrique</strong> on land that belongs to the town hall.\r\n\r\nOn 17 July, the directors made a visit to the site in the presence of the mayor of the municipality, Hon. PISSIYOU Sami Essokudjowu and his deputies.\r\n\r\n</div>'),(13398,993,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13399,993,'block_0_fields',''),(13400,993,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(13401,993,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(13402,993,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(13403,993,'_wp_old_slug','afrique-du-sud-certification-broad-based-black-economic-empowerment'),(13404,993,'_yoast_wpseo_title','TOGO : ERES funds reforestation of 2 hectares'),(13405,993,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Reforestation in northern Togo in the municipality of Kozah.'),(13406,993,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(13407,993,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13408,993,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','138'),(13409,993,'_thumbnail_id','676'),(13411,993,'post_imgs',''),(13412,993,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(13413,993,'_dp_original','675'),(13414,993,'_edit_lock','1635784131:2'),(13415,993,'_edit_last','2'),(13417,993,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13418,993,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Togo'),(13419,993,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','51'),(13423,994,'is_block_prd','0'),(13424,994,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13425,994,'is_block_map','0'),(13426,994,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13427,994,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13428,994,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13429,994,'header_page_text','The Madagascan Committee of Butane has just signed a partnership agreement with the Madagascan authorities for the democratisation of the use of butane gas in Madagascar.'),(13430,994,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(13431,994,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(13432,994,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(13433,994,'header_page_img','678'),(13434,994,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(13435,994,'header_page',''),(13436,994,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(13437,994,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','60'),(13438,994,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(13439,994,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(13440,994,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(13441,994,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(13442,994,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-23'),(13443,994,'block_0_fields_text','<div id=\"Tdet\">\r\n\r\nJuly 2021\r\n\r\nPromoting the use of butane gas as the main alternative energy to charcoal in Madagascar: this is the commitment made by the Ministry of the Environment and Sustainable Development, the Ministry of the Economy and Finance of Madagascar, and the <strong>Madagascan Committee of Butane</strong> (CMDB), the professional group of the butane gas sector in Madagascar, of which <strong>VITOGAZ Madagascar and GALANA Oil Distribution</strong> are part, through a tripartite partnership agreement signed on 2 July.\r\n\r\nThe situation of environmental degradation in Madagascar has become more than alarming in recent years. Coal production is one of the main causes of deforestation, with an annual consumption of 450,000 tonnes of charcoal. This initiative to democratise Butane gas allows actors in the sector to thus taunt the main and harmful competitor of butane: charcoal.\r\n\r\nAfter several years of advocacy with the authorities for a policy revising the reduction of VAT on gas, CMDB and the latter are committed to democratising the use of gas in Madagascan households through various actions: a reduction in the price of the bottle, the marketing of bottles with a smaller capacity, the facilitation of access to gas for new users through allocations and promotions on fatapera kits (cooking set), the development of retail gas sales, and finally the implementation of reforestation campaigns. These commitments will be accompanied by communication and educational actions on the benefits of gas.\r\n\r\nIn a country like Madagascar, such an initiative is a good example of a win-win partnership on all fronts, both for the public sector and the private sector, and finally for Madagascar’s forests, with the result of reducing household carbon emissions.\r\n\r\n</div>'),(13444,994,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13445,994,'block_0_fields',''),(13446,994,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(13447,994,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(13448,994,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(13449,994,'_wp_old_slug','afrique-du-sud-certification-broad-based-black-economic-empowerment'),(1345