pprobation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(13453,994,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13454,994,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','138'),(13455,994,'_thumbnail_id','678'),(13457,994,'post_imgs',''),(13458,994,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(13459,994,'_dp_original','677'),(13460,994,'_edit_lock','1635851148:2'),(13461,994,'_edit_last','2'),(13463,994,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13464,994,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Madagascar'),(13465,994,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','43'),(13467,994,'_wp_old_slug','madagascar-butane-helps-protect-the-madagascan-forest'),(13468,995,'is_block_prd','0'),(13469,995,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13470,995,'is_block_map','0'),(13471,995,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13472,995,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13473,995,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13474,995,'header_page_text','<strong>EcoHeat100</strong> - A 100% renewable domestic fuel oil\r\n\r\nLaunch of the EcoHeat100, a renewable domestic fuel oil capable of reducing carbon emissions over its entire life cycle by up to 90%.'),(13475,995,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(13476,995,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(13477,995,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(13478,995,'header_page_img','601'),(13479,995,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(13480,995,'header_page',''),(13481,995,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(13482,995,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(13483,995,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(13484,995,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(13485,995,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(13486,995,'block_0_fields_text','July 2021\r\n\r\nAt Rubis Energie, we are taking steps with you towards a greener future, offering an immediate solution to reduce the carbon emissions of fuel-heated households and businesses in the Channel Islands.\r\n\r\nRubis Channel Islands (F.S.C.I) is the first fuel distributor to offer renewable domestic fuel oil in Britain. We are at the forefront of the transition to local liquid energy, are fully aligned with the intention of both islands to become carbon neutral and have been working with the government on how to achieve this.\r\n\r\nWe believe that if a customer wants to be carbon neutral, they should have a choice between several energy suppliers and not have to spend thousands of pounds on a new heating system. EcoHeat100 allows domestic fuel customers to do just that: change fuel rather than change their entire heating system. Although the EcoHeat100 is slightly more expensive than traditional fuel oil, for those looking to switch to another electricity to be more environmentally friendly, we now have a more cost-effective option than installing a new electric heating system.\r\n\r\nYou can compare the running costs of EcoHeat100 compared with other energy sources in our helpful table here, see how much you can save on EcoHeat100 compared to gas or electricity.\r\n\r\nRubis EcoHeat100 is a renewable heating oil that can directly replace kerosene or diesel oil and is a pragmatic alternative to less environmentally friendly domestic heating. An excellent choice for combating climate change, EcoHeat100 is just as effective as your usual fuel oil and reduces carbon emissions by 90% during its life cycle. At the local level, we will benefit from better air quality, thanks to the cleaner properties of the EcoHeat100, we will benefit from a reduction in hydrocarbons, NOx, carbon monoxide and particles.\r\n\r\nIt is a hydrotreated vegetable oil (HVO), a second-generation biofuel of superior quality made from renewable and sustainable raw materials, such as used cooking oils and residual fats. It has been successfully tested by Rubis Channel Islands and OFTEC in the UK, demonstrating the huge potential of this oil to help meet the challenge of decarbonising homes and offices. This renewable liquid fuel adapts to all existing fuel oil heating systems, thanks to a simple and cost-effective conversion process that will take no more than one morning to switch you to this fuel.\r\n\r\nIn addition to local and global environmental benefits, with EcoHEat100 you will continue to enjoy the warmth and comfort that fuel heating systems bring to your home.\r\n\r\nGlobally, and closer to home, targets and plans have been set to achieve net zero carbon. We believe that if we act together, we can act more quickly and make a difference, regardless of the scale of our approach. With a growing range of sustainable products for your vehicles and now for your homes and businesses, we are committed to helping shape a greener future.'),(13487,995,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13488,995,'block_0_fields',''),(13489,995,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(13490,995,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(13491,995,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(13492,995,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-channel-islands-fuel-ecoheat-100'),(13493,995,'_yoast_wpseo_title','CHANNEL ISLANDS: launch of fuel oil EcoHeat100'),(13494,995,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Launch of the EcoHeat100, a renewable domestic fuel oil capable of reducing carbon emissions over its entire life cycle by up to 90%.'),(13495,995,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(13496,995,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13497,995,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','136'),(13498,995,'_thumbnail_id','601'),(13500,995,'post_imgs',''),(13501,995,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(13502,995,'_dp_original','599'),(13503,995,'_edit_lock','1635773371:2'),(13504,995,'_edit_last','2'),(13506,995,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13507,995,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Channel Islands'),(13508,995,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','42'),(13509,996,'is_block_prd','0'),(13510,996,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13511,996,'is_block_map','0'),(13512,996,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13513,996,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13514,996,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13515,996,'header_page_text','VITOGAZ EXPRESS: when innovation serves our customers and reduces our carbon footprint.'),(13516,996,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(13517,996,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(13518,996,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(13519,996,'header_page_img','686'),(13520,996,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(13521,996,'header_page',''),(13522,996,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(13523,996,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(13524,996,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(13525,996,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(13526,996,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(13527,996,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(13528,996,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-23'),(13529,996,'block_0_fields_text','May 2021\r\n\r\n<strong>VITOGAZ MADAGASCAR </strong>innove dans la capitale malgache en lançant un service inédit de livraison de bouteilles de gaz en vélo électrique.\r\n\r\nRésolument orienté Client, Vitogaz répond ainsi aux besoins du consommateur en période de confinement tout en réduisant son empreinte carbone. Depuis quelques semaines, les consommateurs de gaz de la capitale Antananarivo peuvent commander leur bouteille de gaz et/ou accessoires, et se faire livrer directement chez eux, à travers la nouvelle offre de service <strong>VITOGAZ EXPRESS</strong>.\r\n\r\nUne flotte de cinq vélos cargo, fonctionnant à l’électricité, a été mise en place en partenariat avec <strong>Mbike Livraison Express</strong>, une société de livraison à vélo qui dispose aussi d’une plateforme de vente en ligne, ainsi que le réseau de stations-services Jovena. Sur simple appel téléphonique, par un message sur facebook ou via la plateforme de vente en ligne dédiée, les clients peuvent bénéficier de ce service innovant de livraison, et avec un cout de livraison symbolique à 3.000 ariarys (moins de 1 euro).   Dans le contexte actuel de crise sanitaire, avec une limitation des déplacements et des mouvements, les confinements pendant les week-ends pour Antananarivo, cette offre tombe à pic pour les consommateurs. Elle facilite aussi leur vie en leur évitant la corvée des bouteilles jusqu’à leurs points de vente habituels. Enfin, ce service constitue un plus pour l’environnement, réduisant l’impact carbone pour la distribution de gaz.\r\n\r\nCette initiative renforce la volonté de la société Vitogaz de promouvoir le gaz, en facilitant son utilisation, son acquisition par les consommateurs. Pour rappel, à Madagascar, le développement du marché des Gaz liquéfiés est un réel enjeu car il permet de réduire l’utilisation du charbon de bois, une menace sévère pour la forêt et l’environnement en général.\r\n\r\n<strong>VITOGAZ MADAGASCAR</strong> is innovating in the Madagascan capital by launching an innovative electric bicycle gas bottle delivery service.\r\n\r\nVitogaz is firmly customer-oriented and thus meets the needs of consumers during lockdown periods while reducing their carbon footprint. For the past few weeks, gas consumers in the capital Antananarivo can order their gas bottle and/or accessories, and have them delivered directly to their homes, through the new <strong>VITOGAZ EXPRESS</strong> service offer.\r\n\r\nA fleet of five electric cargo bikes has been set up in partnership with <strong>Mbike Delivery Express</strong>, a bike delivery company that also has an online sales platform, as well as the Jovena service station network. Customers can benefit from this innovative delivery service, and with a symbolic delivery cost of 3,000 ariary (less than 1 euro) following a simple phone call, by message on Facebook or via the dedicated online sales platform.   Given the current healthcare crisis, with restrictions on travel and movement, and weekend lockdowns for Antananarivo, this offer has come at exactly the right time for our customers. It also makes their lives easier by avoiding the chore of taking bottles to their usual points of sale. Finally, this service is a plus for the environment, reducing the carbon impact for gas retail.\r\n\r\nThis initiative strengthens Vitogaz\'s desire to promote gas by facilitating its use and acquisition by consumers. As a reminder, in Madagascar, the development of the liquefied gas market is a real challenge because it reduces the use of charcoal – a severe threat to the forest and the environment in general.'),(13530,996,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13531,996,'block_0_fields',''),(13532,996,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(13533,996,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(13534,996,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(13535,996,'_wp_old_slug','afrique-du-sud-certification-broad-based-black-economic-empowerment'),(13536,996,'_yoast_wpseo_title','MADAGASCAR: launch of an unprecedented service for the delivery of gas cylinders by electric bike.'),(13537,996,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','VITOGAZ EXPRESS: when innovation serves our customers and reduces our carbon footprint.'),(13538,996,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(13539,996,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13540,996,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','138'),(13541,996,'_thumbnail_id','686'),(13543,996,'post_imgs',''),(13544,996,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(13545,996,'_dp_original','679'),(13546,996,'_edit_lock','1635931796:2'),(13547,996,'_edit_last','2'),(13549,996,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13550,996,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Madagascar'),(13551,996,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','33'),(13553,997,'_thumbnail_id','688'),(13554,997,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13555,997,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13556,997,'is_block_prd','0'),(13557,997,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13558,997,'is_block_map','0'),(13559,997,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13560,997,'header_page_text','Rubis Bahamas awarded $6,500 in scholarships.'),(13561,997,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(13562,997,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(13563,997,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(13564,997,'header_page_img','688'),(13565,997,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(13566,997,'header_page',''),(13567,997,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(13568,997,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','60'),(13569,997,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(13570,997,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','138'),(13571,997,'_yoast_wpseo_title','BAHAMAS: awarding of scholarships'),(13572,997,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','In line with its commitment to education and youth in the Bahamas and as part of its commitment to education and youth there, Rubis Bahamas provided the Bahamas Debutante Foundation and the Bahamas Primary School Student of The Year Foundation with $6,500 in scholarships as part of this global pandemic.'),(13573,997,'block_0_fields_text','May 2021\r\n\r\nIn line with its commitment to education and youth in the Bahamas and as part of its commitment to education and youth there, <strong>Rubis Bahamas</strong> provided <strong>the Bahamas Debutante Foundation</strong> and <strong>the Bahamas Primary School Student of The Year Foundation</strong> with $6,500 in scholarships as part of this global pandemic.\r\n\r\nThe realities of COVID-19 have had an impact on all sectors of the economy in Bahamas within increased pressure being placed on families.\r\n\r\n<em>“Rubis cares about every community in which we operate and the youth of our nation. We recognise and reward the diligence and perseverance of these students in their quest for success. Their years of hard work and sacrifice must not go unnoticed despite the challenges and setbacks faced by Covid-19. We will continue to contribute to the growth and development of Bahamian excellence,”</em> said Latia Duncombe, Director of Sales and Marketing at Rubis Bahamas.\r\n\r\nThe Bahamas Debutante Foundation and the Bahamas Primary School Student of The Year Foundation are two important organisations dedicated to educating Bahamian students and ensuring that they are recognised and rewarded for their outstanding achievements. Funds donated by Rubis are used to provide scholarships to deserving students. As a responsible company, Rubis hopes to encourage students to excel.\r\n\r\nIn a letter of thanks, Demian Brice II (one of the winners) wrote: <em>\'As the world faces challenging economic times, I congratulate Rubis on continuing to invest in the future of students like me. The scholarship will be used to pay my tuition at St. Augustine’s College. Please be assured that I intend to continue to strive for academic excellence in pursuing my dream of becoming an engineer.”</em>'),(13574,997,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13575,997,'block_0_fields',''),(13576,997,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(13577,997,'_wp_old_slug','galana-participe-foire-internationale-madagascar'),(13579,997,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-23'),(13580,997,'post_imgs',''),(13581,997,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(13582,997,'_dp_original','687'),(13583,997,'_edit_lock','1635774319:2'),(13584,997,'_edit_last','2'),(13586,997,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13587,997,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Bahamas'),(13588,997,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','47'),(13590,998,'_wp_attached_file','Rubis_CSR-roadmap_2022_2025_EN.pdf'),(13591,999,'_thumbnail_id','690'),(13592,999,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13593,999,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13594,999,'is_block_prd','0'),(13595,999,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13596,999,'is_block_map','0'),(13597,999,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13598,999,'header_page_text','The young Madagascan start-up supported by Rubis Mécénat has managed to be successful.'),(13599,999,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(13600,999,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(13601,999,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(13602,999,'header_page_img','690'),(13603,999,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(13604,999,'header_page',''),(13605,999,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(13606,999,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(13607,999,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(13608,999,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','138'),(13609,999,'_yoast_wpseo_title','MADAGASCAR: How a young Madagascan start-up managed to win'),(13610,999,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','The young Madagascan start-up supported by Rubis Mécénat has succeeded in making work jackets from plastic recycling. Vests worn by VITOGAZ Madagascan employees.'),(13611,999,'block_0_fields_text','May 2021\r\n\r\n<strong>The young Madagascan start-up supported by Rubis Mécénat has succeeded in making work jackets from plastic recycling. Vests worn by VITOGAZ Madagascan employees.</strong>\r\n\r\nProduction of fleece work jackets with Polyfloss wool, products from plastic recycling, for VITOGAZ Madagascan employees is a win for the young people of NDAO HANAVAO and <strong>VITOGAZ Madagascar</strong>.\r\n\r\nAs the southern winter approaches, the VITOGAZ Madagascan teams have just received their new work clothing: a fleece jacket with polyfloss wool, produced by <strong>R’ART PLAST</strong>, a start-up created by young people in integration at the NDAO HANAVAO innovation laboratory (“let’s innovate” in Madagascar). NDAO HANAVAO is an innovation and creation laboratory for social design, initiated by <strong>RUBIS MECENAT</strong>, with the involvement of VITOGAZ Madagascar. Created in 2018, this laboratory welcomes young people from disadvantaged backgrounds in Antananarivo, through a social integration programme, with training in personal development, language, entrepreneurship and design, in conjunction with local and international designers. The purpose of the laboratory is to promote the manufacture of wool from recycling of plastic waste using a unique process: <strong>POLYFLOSS</strong>.\r\n\r\nSince 2020, young people, at the end of their vocational training, have created a company to produce and market their products: this is how R’ART PLAST was born. The young company continues to research design, combining traditional and modern techniques, offering a variety of innovative and useful products. This is how she supplied the wool used to fleece the work jackets ordered by VITOGAZ Madagascar.\r\n\r\nFor VITOGAZ Madagascar, this initiative strengthens the desire to promote its societal actions both in terms of environmental protection and socially through Ndao Hanavao. Each employee is thus made aware of and mobilised on the values of society.'),(13612,999,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13613,999,'block_0_fields',''),(13614,999,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(13615,999,'_wp_old_slug','galana-participe-foire-internationale-madagascar'),(13616,999,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-23'),(13618,999,'post_imgs',''),(13619,999,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(13620,999,'_dp_original','689'),(13621,999,'_edit_lock','1635784068:2'),(13622,999,'_edit_last','2'),(13624,999,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13625,999,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Madagascar'),(13626,999,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','37'),(13628,999,'_wp_old_slug','madagascar-how-a-young-madagascan-start-up-managed-to-win'),(13630,1000,'is_block_prd','0'),(13631,1000,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13632,1000,'is_block_map','0'),(13633,1000,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13634,1000,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13635,1000,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13636,1000,'header_page_text','Vitogas Espana donated to the Barcelona Clinic Hospital and the José Carreras Foundation.'),(13637,1000,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(13638,1000,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(13639,1000,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(13640,1000,'header_page_img','464'),(13641,1000,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(13642,1000,'header_page',''),(13643,1000,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(13644,1000,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(13645,1000,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(13646,1000,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(13647,1000,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(13648,1000,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(13649,1000,'block_0_fields_text','May 2021\r\n\r\n<strong>Vitogas Espana</strong> wanted to collaborate in the fight against coronavirus by making a financial contribution to <strong>the Clínic-IDIBAPS Hospital</strong> in Barcelona and to <strong>the Josep Carreras Foundation</strong> for Leukaemia.\r\n\r\nThanks to donations received from individuals and companies, the research teams and health professionals at Clínic-IDIBAPS Hospital will be able to continue to progress in obtaining answers that will help them better understand the SARS-CoV coronavirus and its behaviour.\r\n\r\nVitogas’ contribution will also be paid to the José Carreras Foundation, of which it is an associate partner. Specifically, the money will be used to fund a programme to support families and patients with leukaemia, one of the diseases most affected by the global pandemic. Extreme isolation and severe restrictions caused by coronavirus have resulted in haematological patients experiencing isolation and lack of psychosocial care, which requires immediate resolution with the implementation of such initiatives.\r\n\r\nAgainst this challenging background caused by the pandemic, collaborations such as those of Vitogas are a boost for health entities to continue to have the resources needed to improve the care of patients in emergency situations and, in turn, to advance research against COVID-19.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;'),(13650,1000,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13651,1000,'block_0_fields',''),(13652,1000,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(13653,1000,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(13654,1000,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(13655,1000,'_wp_old_slug','espagne-vitogas-3eme-edition-festival-montgolfieres'),(13656,1000,'_yoast_wpseo_title','Rubis Energie - Vitogas spain supports research against COVID-19'),(13657,1000,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Vitogas Espana donated to the Barcelona Clinic Hospital and the José Carreras Foundation.'),(13658,1000,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(13659,1000,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13660,1000,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','138'),(13661,1000,'_thumbnail_id','486'),(13663,1000,'post_imgs',''),(13664,1000,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(13665,1000,'_dp_original','585'),(13666,1000,'_edit_lock','1635784565:2'),(13667,1000,'_edit_last','2'),(13669,1000,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13670,1000,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Spain'),(13671,1000,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','32'),(13672,1001,'is_block_prd','0'),(13673,1001,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13674,1001,'is_block_map','0'),(13675,1001,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13676,1001,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13677,1001,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13678,1001,'header_page_text','Rubis Energia Portugal becomes the exclusive partner for the marketing of liquefied gas in the Q8 service station network.'),(13679,1001,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(13680,1001,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(13681,1001,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(13682,1001,'header_page_img','607'),(13683,1001,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(13684,1001,'header_page',''),(13685,1001,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(13686,1001,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(13687,1001,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(13688,1001,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(13689,1001,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(13690,1001,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(13691,1001,'block_0_fields_text','April 2021\r\n\r\nWe are very pleased to announce the new partnership between the VAPO – Q8 Group and the Rubis group in Portugal with its trademark, Rubis Gas.\r\n\r\nThanks to this new partnership, all Q8 service stations in Portugal will exclusively sell gas cylinders (butane and propane) as well as Rubis Gas liquefied gas.\r\n\r\nThe VAPO – Q8 Group is convinced that this is another important step for the growth and reputation of the brand in Portugal.\r\n\r\n“In the search for continuous improvement, Q8 is establishing a partnership with the Rubis Group in Portugal that will exclusively supply the network of service stations. Rubis Gas, as the leader in customer satisfaction in the bottled gas sector, represents added value, with Q8, to better serve their customers\", are the words of Joaquim Gonçalves, CEO of the Vapo Group.'),(13692,1001,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13693,1001,'block_0_fields',''),(13694,1001,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(13695,1001,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(13696,1001,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(13697,1001,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-channel-islands-fuel-ecoheat-100'),(13698,1001,'_yoast_wpseo_title','Rubis Energia Portugal signs partnership with the Q8 network'),(13699,1001,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Rubis Energia Portugal becomes the exclusive partner for the marketing of liquefied gas in the Q8 service station network.'),(13700,1001,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le dével