t compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(13977,1007,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(13978,1007,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','138'),(13979,1007,'_thumbnail_id','781'),(13980,1007,'post_imgs',''),(13981,1007,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(13982,1007,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Liberia'),(13983,1007,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','28'),(13985,1007,'_dp_original','780'),(13986,1007,'_edit_lock','1635787863:2'),(13987,1007,'_edit_last','2'),(13989,1007,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(13991,1007,'_wp_old_slug','senegal-eres-senegal-finances-the-drilling-of-a-well'),(13992,1008,'is_block_prd','0'),(13993,1008,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(13994,1008,'is_block_map','0'),(13995,1008,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(13996,1008,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(13997,1008,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(13998,1008,'header_page_text','Rubis Asphalt Middle East has launched the construction of a new bitumen vessel with a capacity of 15,000 DWT, called the BITU RIVER.'),(13999,1008,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(14000,1008,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(14001,1008,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(14002,1008,'header_page_img','746'),(14003,1008,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(14004,1008,'header_page',''),(14005,1008,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(14006,1008,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(14007,1008,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(14008,1008,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(14009,1008,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(14010,1008,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(14011,1008,'_wp_old_date','2021-10-11'),(14012,1008,'block_0_fields_text','September 2020\r\n\r\nThe<strong> BITU RIVER</strong> will be designed by FKAB Marine Design, built by China Merchants Jinling Shipyard (Yangzhou) Dingheng Co. Ltd and classified by RINA.\r\n\r\nThe shipbuilding contract was signed in July 2020 and delivery is planned for mid-2022.\r\n\r\nThe bitumen can carry 15,000 tonnes of bitumen. It is a bitumen specially designed for the shallow waters of the Gulf of Guinea, and in particular, the rivers of Nigeria.\r\n\r\nIt will be equipped with an electric diesel drive, driving 2 360° omnidirectional thrusters for better handling.\r\n\r\nThe vessel will have fully insulated bitumen tanks, with bitumen to be maintained at a temperature of 140 to 150°C.\r\n\r\nThis new vessel construction will complement our bitumen fleet and help consolidate our position as the leading bitumen supplier in Africa.\r\n<div class=\"news-dtls-img\"></div>\r\n&nbsp;'),(14013,1008,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(14014,1008,'block_0_fields',''),(14015,1008,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(14016,1008,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(14017,1008,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(14018,1008,'_wp_old_slug','pole-bitume-nouveau-bitumier-en-construction'),(14019,1008,'_yoast_wpseo_title','BITUMEN POLE: New bitumen vessel under construction'),(14020,1008,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Rubis Asphalt Middle East a lancé la construction d\'un nouveau navire bitumier d’une capacité de 15 000 DWT, nommé le BITU RIVER.'),(14021,1008,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(14022,1008,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(14023,1008,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','136'),(14024,1008,'_thumbnail_id','746'),(14025,1008,'post_imgs',''),(14026,1008,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(14027,1008,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Rubis bitumen pole'),(14028,1008,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','33'),(14030,1008,'_dp_original','745'),(14031,1008,'_edit_lock','1635788213:2'),(14032,1008,'_edit_last','2'),(14034,1008,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(14035,1009,'is_block_prd','0'),(14036,1009,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(14037,1009,'is_block_map','0'),(14038,1009,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(14039,1009,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(14040,1009,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(14041,1009,'header_page_text','Scholarships for 10 undergraduate students in the district of Sapele Okpe, Delta region'),(14042,1009,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(14043,1009,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(14044,1009,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(14045,1009,'header_page_img','574'),(14046,1009,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(14047,1009,'header_page',''),(14048,1009,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(14049,1009,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(14050,1009,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(14051,1009,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(14052,1009,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(14053,1009,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(14054,1009,'block_0_fields_text','August 2020\r\n\r\nAs part of <strong>Ringardas Nigeria</strong> Limited’s corporate social responsibility to pay attention to the host communities where we operate, Ringardas Nigeria Limited has awarded a scholarship to 10 undergraduate students in the Sapele Okpe community.\r\n\r\nThese students are currently studying at public and private universities in Nigeria.\r\n\r\nOur goal is to support the winners throughout their studies so that they can easily achieve their career aspirations and contribute positively to society.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n&nbsp;'),(14055,1009,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(14056,1009,'block_0_fields',''),(14057,1009,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(14058,1009,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(14059,1009,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(14060,1009,'_yoast_wpseo_title','NIGERIA: Awarding of a scholarship to 10 students'),(14061,1009,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Scholarships for 10 undergraduate students in the district of Sapele Okpe, Delta region'),(14062,1009,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(14063,1009,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(14064,1009,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','138'),(14065,1009,'_thumbnail_id','574'),(14067,1009,'post_imgs',''),(14068,1009,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(14069,1009,'_dp_original','572'),(14070,1009,'_edit_lock','1635788526:2'),(14071,1009,'_edit_last','2'),(14073,1009,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(14074,1009,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Nigeria'),(14075,1009,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','42'),(14077,1009,'_wp_old_slug','nigeria-awarding-of-a-scholarship-to-10-students'),(14078,1010,'is_block_prd','0'),(14079,1010,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(14080,1010,'is_block_map','0'),(14081,1010,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(14082,1010,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(14083,1010,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(14084,1010,'header_page_text','The VITO network supports you to improve the comfort of your home over the long term under the slogan “Engagé pour FAIRE”.'),(14085,1010,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(14086,1010,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(14087,1010,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(14088,1010,'header_page_img','970'),(14089,1010,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(14090,1010,'header_page',''),(14091,1010,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(14092,1010,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(14093,1010,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(14094,1010,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(14095,1010,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(14096,1010,'block_0_fields_text','March 2020\r\n\r\nOn 25 March 2020, the SRPP undertakes and signs the FAIRE charter: Facilitating, Supporting and Informing for Energy Renovation.\r\n\r\nBy signing the FAIRE charter and adopting the \"Engagé pour FAIRE \" signature, the SRPP confirms its commitment and renews its pledge of trust with all players in energy renovation who have also chosen to commit to this approach.\r\n\r\n<em>Engagé pour FAIRE = Committed to DO</em>'),(14097,1010,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(14098,1010,'block_0_fields',''),(14099,1010,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(14100,1010,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(14101,1010,'_yoast_wpseo_title','LA REUNION: SRPP joins the \"FAIRE\" network'),(14102,1010,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','Under the slogan \"Engage pour FAIRE\", the VITO network supports you in improving the comfort of your home in the long term.'),(14103,1010,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(14104,1010,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(14105,1010,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','138'),(14107,1010,'post_imgs',''),(14108,1010,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(14109,1010,'_thumbnail_id','970'),(14110,1010,'_dp_original','549'),(14111,1010,'_edit_lock','1635789097:2'),(14112,1010,'_edit_last','2'),(14114,1010,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(14116,1011,'is_block_prd','0'),(14117,1011,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(14118,1011,'is_block_map','0'),(14119,1011,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(14120,1011,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(14121,1011,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(14122,1011,'header_page_text','The Rubis Group is submitting a takeover bid for KenolKobil, the leading distributor of petroleum products in Kenya, but also established in Burundi, Ethiopia, Uganda, Rwanda and Zambia.'),(14123,1011,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(14124,1011,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(14125,1011,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(14126,1011,'header_page_img','768'),(14127,1011,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(14128,1011,'header_page',''),(14129,1011,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(14130,1011,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','60'),(14131,1011,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(14133,1011,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(14134,1011,'block_0_fields_text','October 2018\r\n\r\n<strong>Following the acquisition of 24.99% of the capital of KenolKobil Plc, the Rubis Group today announced its intention to launch a public tender offer on the remaining capital, in accordance with the regulations applicable to the Nairobi Stock Exchange, the Kenyan Capital Markets Act and all other applicable laws and regulations.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, the leader in the distribution of petroleum products in Kenya, is also established in Burundi, Ethiopia, Uganda, Rwanda and Zambia with a total volume in final distribution of 1.3 million m3 in 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil encompasses all oil product distribution activities: networks (350 service stations), aviation fuels, liquefied gas, lubricants, bitumen, with secure access to pipelines and its mesh of 10 terminals.\r\n\r\nThe petroleum products distribution sector in East Africa is benefiting from steady growth in demand, driven by demographic development, urbanisation and investments in road infrastructure. With a population pool of more than 200 million inhabitants, KenolKobil offers solid development prospects.\r\n\r\nSince 2013, KenolKobil has recorded steady growth in its volumes and results with a normalised operating income of USD 50 million generated in 2017 and has a solid financial structure.\r\n\r\nAt KES 23 (Kenyan Shillings) per share, Rubis’ bid valued KenolKobil at USD 353 million (100%), financed by the Group’s own resources with an immediate accretive effect.\r\n\r\nThe final launch of the public tender offer is subject to the approval of the regional and national competition authorities and any other competent authority.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil perfectly matches the Rubis Group’s investment objectives and criteria and will ideally complement Rubis Energie’s position in Africa, in a particularly promising sector where the Group intends to provide new impetus.\r\n<p data-wp-editing=\"1\"><img class=\"alignnone wp-image-950\" src=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/Rubis-Energy-Uganda-quad_RVB-300x172.jpg\" alt=\"Logo Rubis Uganda\" width=\"114\" height=\"66\" /> <img class=\"alignnone wp-image-951\" src=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/Rubis-Energy-Zambia-quad_RVB-300x172.jpg\" alt=\"Logo Rubis Zambia\" width=\"113\" height=\"65\" /> <img class=\"alignnone wp-image-949\" src=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/Rubis-Energy-Rwanda-quad_RVB-300x172.jpg\" alt=\"Logo Rubis Rwanda\" width=\"113\" height=\"65\" /> <img class=\"alignnone wp-image-948\" src=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/Rubis-Energy-Kenya-quad_RVB-300x172.jpg\" alt=\"Logo Rubis Kenya\" width=\"115\" height=\"66\" /> <img class=\"alignnone wp-image-947\" src=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/Rubis-Energy-Ethiopia-quad_RVB-300x172.jpg\" alt=\"Logo Rubis Ethiopia\" width=\"115\" height=\"66\" /> <img class=\"alignnone wp-image-946\" src=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/Rubis-Energy-Burundi-quad_RVB-300x172.jpg\" alt=\"Logos Rubis Burundi\" width=\"113\" height=\"65\" /></p>'),(14135,1011,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(14136,1011,'block_0_fields',''),(14137,1011,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(14138,1011,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(14139,1011,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-afrique-est'),(14140,1011,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-afrique-est-kenolkobil'),(14141,1011,'_yoast_wpseo_title','EAST AFRICA: The Rubis Group takes positions'),(14142,1011,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','The Rubis Group is submitting a takeover bid for KenolKobil, the leading distributor of petroleum products in Kenya, but also established in Burundi, Ethiopia, Uganda, Rwanda and Zambia.'),(14143,1011,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(14144,1011,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(14145,1011,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','136'),(14146,1011,'_thumbnail_id','768'),(14147,1011,'post_imgs',''),(14148,1011,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(14149,1011,'_dp_original','58'),(14150,1011,'_edit_lock','1635789476:2'),(14151,1011,'_edit_last','2'),(14153,1011,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(14154,1011,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','East Africa'),(14155,1011,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','38'),(14157,1011,'_wp_old_slug','east-africa-the-rubis-group-takes-positions'),(14158,1012,'is_block_prd','0'),(14159,1012,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(14160,1012,'is_block_map','0'),(14161,1012,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(14162,1012,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(14163,1012,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(14164,1012,'header_page_text','The Rubis Group buys liquefied gas distribution assets from REPSOL.'),(14165,1012,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(14166,1012,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(14167,1012,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(14168,1012,'header_page_img','771'),(14169,1012,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(14170,1012,'header_page',''),(14171,1012,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(14172,1012,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(14173,1012,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(14174,1012,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(14175,1012,'block_0_fields_text','July 2017\r\n\r\nIt was in the Portuguese islands of Madeira and the Azores that the Rubis Group acquired the Repsol liquefied gas distribution assets, as well as the continental channelled distribution networks.\r\n\r\nThis acquisition expands the Rubis Group’s offering to the channelled networks segment and enables it to reach a critical size in its existing activities in Madeira and the Azores.\r\n\r\nRepresenting around an annual volume of 15,000 tonnes, these activities generate normative gross operating income (EBITDA) of around €6 million.\r\n\r\nThe assets acquired comprise different segments: packaging, bulk and channelled distribution networks as well as the related operational facilities.\r\n\r\nThrough this new acquisition, the Rubis Group remains faithful to its development strategy in market niches complementary to its existing activities.'),(14176,1012,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(14177,1012,'block_0_fields',''),(14178,1012,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(14179,1012,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest'),(14180,1012,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-position-portugal'),(14181,1012,'_yoast_wpseo_title','Portugal: Rubis strengthens its position in Portugal'),(14182,1012,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','The Rubis Group buys liquefied gas distribution assets from REPSOL.'),(14183,1012,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','136'),(14184,1012,'post_imgs',''),(14185,1012,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(14186,1012,'_thumbnail_id','771'),(14187,1012,'_dp_original','55'),(14188,1012,'_edit_lock','1635789754:2'),(14189,1012,'_edit_last','2'),(14191,1012,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(14193,1012,'_wp_old_slug','portugal-rubis-strengthens-its-position-in-portugal'),(14194,1013,'is_block_prd','0'),(14195,1013,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(14196,1013,'is_block_map','0'),(14197,1013,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(14198,1013,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(14199,1013,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(14200,1013,'header_page_text','The Rubis Group acquired the Galana Group, the leading distributor of petroleum products in Madagascar.'),(14201,1013,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(14202,1013,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(14203,1013,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(14204,1013,'header_page_img','787'),(14205,1013,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(14206,1013,'header_page',''),(14207,1013,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(14208,1013,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(14209,1013,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(14211,1013,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(14212,1013,'block_0_fields_text','July 2017\r\n\r\n<strong>The Galana Group</strong>, active in key market segments such as fuels, liquefied gases and lubricants and with a network of 71 service stations, distributed 260,000 m3 of petroleum products in 2016 for a turnover of $215 million.\r\n\r\nThanks to dedicated maritime access, the Group has a strategic and autonomous logistics tool, consisting of the island’s only oil product import storage facility in Tamatave (260,000 m3).\r\n\r\nWith a 30% market share combined with a unique logistics position, Galana combines, through its leading position, all the strategic criteria sought by the Rubis Group. Through the acquisition of Galana, the latter significantly increases its presence in the distribution of petroleum products in the Indian Ocean.\r\n\r\nThe increased volumes in this growing region should ultimately generate economies of scale (trading and shipping) for the Rubis Group.'),(14213,1013,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(14214,1013,'block_0_fields',''),(14215,1013,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(14216,1013,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-2'),(14217,1013,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-renforce-presence-madagascar'),(14218,1013,'_yoast_wpseo_title','MADAGASCAR: Rubis strengthens its presence'),(14219,1013,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','The Rubis Group acquired the Galana Group, the leading distributor of petroleum products in Madagascar.'),(14220,1013,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','136'),(14221,1013,'post_imgs',''),(14222,1013,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(14223,1013,'_thumbnail_id','787'),(14224,1013,'_dp_original','56'),(14225,1013,'_edit_lock','1635790014:2'),(14226,1013,'_edit_last','2'),(14228,1013,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(14229,1013,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Madagascar'),(14230,1013,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','39'),(14231,1014,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-09'),(14232,1014,'is_block_prd','0'),(14233,1014,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(14234,1014,'is_block_map','0'),(14235,1014,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(14236,1014,'block_0_fields_text','February 2017\r\n\r\nWith 600,000 m3 distributed, Dinasa, Haiti\'s leading network of service stations (125 stations), operates under the \"NATIONAL\" brand and operates in all segments of the oil product offering, with a leading position in the marketing of aviation fuels, liquefied gas, commercial fuel oil and lubricants.\r\n\r\nThe company has a strategic and autonomous import logistics tool (storage, maritime access).\r\n\r\nDinasa combines the main strategic criteria sought by Rubis in distribution: a leading position in a niche market associated with controlling its supply logistics.\r\n\r\nDinasa\'s sales volumes represent an increase of more than 35% in Rubis Energie\'s activity in the Caribbean region and will undoubtedly generate supply levers in perspective (densification of trading in the region combined with economies of scale in shipping).\r\n\r\nDuring the year ended 30 September 2016, the Dinasa Group generated a gross operating income (EBITDA) of €40.4 million.\r\n\r\nThe effective acquisition is scheduled for Q2 2017.'),(14237,1014,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(14238,1014,'block_0_fields',''),(14239,1014,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(14240,1014,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(14241,1014,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(14242,1014,'header_page_text','The Rubis Group has signed an agreement to buy back all the shares of Dinasa and its subsidiary Sodigaz, the leading distributors of petroleum products in Haiti.'),(14243,1014,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(14244,1014,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(14245,1014,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(14246,1014,'header_page_img','613'),(14247,1014,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(14248,1014,'header_page',''),(14249,1014,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(14250,1014,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(14251,1014,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(14252,1014,'_thumbnail_id','613'),(14253,1014,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-arrive-en-haiti'),(14254,1014,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-haiti'),(14255,1014,'_yoast_wpseo_title','HAITI: Rubis Energie is positioning itself'),(14256,1014,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','The Rubis Group has signed an agreement to buy back all the shares of Dinasa and its subsidiary Sodigaz, the leading distributors of petroleum products in Haiti.'),(14257,1014,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','136'),(14258,1014,'post_imgs',''),(14259,1014,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(14260,1014,'_dp_original','210'),(14261,1014,'_edit_lock','1635931915:2'),(14262,1014,'_edit_last','2'),(14264,1014,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(14265,1014,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Haiti'),(14266,1014,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','51'),(14268,1014,'_wp_old_slug','haiti-rubis-energie-is-positioning-itself'),(14269,1015,'is_block_prd','0'),(14270,1015,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(14271,1015,'is_block_map','0'),(14272,1015,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(14273,1015,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(14274,1015,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(14275,1015,'header_page_text','It left the shipyards in mid-October and is now sailing towards the Caribbean seas.'),(14276,1015,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(14277,1015,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(14278,1015,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(14279,1015,'header_page_img','867'),(14280,1015,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(14281,1015,'header_page',''),(14282,1015,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(14283,1015,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(14284,1015,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(14285,1015,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(14286,1015,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(14287,1015,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(14288,1015,'_wp_old_date','2021-10-08'),(14289,1015,'_wp_old_date','2021-10-21'),(14290,1015,'block_0_fields_text','<span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; color: black;\">October 2021</span>\r\n\r\nOn 14 October 2021, Le Morbihan was delivered. It is now sailing towards the Caribbean, its final destination.\r\n\r\nThis vessel, measuring 120 m, weighing 9140 MT and with a capacity of 10,500 m3, will join the fleet of our subsidiary Rubis Eastern Caribbean. It will sail in the Caribbean waters at the beginning of 2022.\r\n\r\nLet\'s wish it well.'),(14291,1015,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(14292,1015,'block_0_fields',''),(14293,1015,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(14294,1015,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(14295,1015,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(14296,1015,'_wp_old_slug','guyane-premiere-centrale-electrique-multi-megawatts-a-hydrogene-au-monde'),(14297,1015,'_yoast_wpseo_title','CARIBBEAN: MORBIHAN, the latest addition to the Rubis fleet'),(14298,1015,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','It left the shipyards in mid-October and is now sailing towards the Caribbean seas.'),(14299,1015,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(14300,1015,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(14301,1015,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','136'),(14302,1015,'_thumbnail_id','867'),(14303,1015,'post_imgs',''),(14304,1015,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(14305,1015,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','CARIBBEAN'),(14306,1015,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','49'),(14308,1015,'_dp_original','864'),(14309,1015,'_edit_lock','1637333097:2'),(14310,1015,'_edit_last','2'),(14312,1015,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(14314,1015,'_wp_old_slug','caribbean-morbihan-the-latest-addition-to-the-rubis-fleet'),(14315,1016,'is_block_prd','0'),(14316,1016,'_is_block_prd','field_60d9cc3911a1c'),(14317,1016,'is_block_map','0'),(14318,1016,'_is_block_map','field_60d9cc5011a1d'),(14319,1016,'block','a:1:{i:0;s:10:\"block.text\";}'),(14320,1016,'_block','field_5d31c1ded5632'),(14321,1016,'header_page_text','The latest project carried out by Ringardas with the financial support of the Rubis Group.'),(14322,1016,'_header_page_text','field_60dad748a56be'),(14323,1016,'header_page_color','#4a58c1'),(14324,1016,'_header_page_color','field_60dad74ca56bf'),(14325,1016,'header_page_img','945'),(14326,1016,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(14327,1016,'header_page',''),(14328,1016,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(14329,1016,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(14330,1016,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(14331,1016,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(14332,1016,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(14333,1016,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(14334,1016,'_wp_old_date','2021-10-08'),(14335,1016,'_wp_old_date','2021-10-12'),(14336,1016,'_wp_old_date','2021-10-26'),(14337,1016,'block_0_fields_text','september 2021\r\n<div id=\"Tdet\">\r\n\r\nAs part of its commitment to social responsibility in the communities where it operates, Ringardas was able to renovate a classroom block at a government school, LEA Primary School in Kurunduma, FCT, Abuja. The school was established in 1976.\r\n\r\nRingardas was able to carry out this project thanks to the financial support of the Rubis Group.\r\n\r\nThe official handover ceremony of the renovated classroom block took place on 22 September 2021. In addition to the renovated classroom block, Ringardas also donated 3 new pedal hand wash units to the same school.\r\n\r\nThe Headmistress was visibly happy and expressed her sincere gratitude on behalf of the school\'s management and students to the management of <strong>Ringardas</strong>. She said that they were particularly happy because no renovation had been done in the school for a very long time. We have waited a long time for this project and now that it is completed, we are grateful and it will be put to good use,\" she said. The benefit we will get from it is unquantifiable.\r\n\r\nRingardas also donated two new pedal handwashing systems to Asokoro Junior Secondary School. The purpose of these systems is to provide students with easy access to handwashing facilities so that they can wash their hands regularly. The aim is to develop a culture of good hygiene habits. This is particularly necessary in these times of COVID-19.\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n</div>'),(14338,1016,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(14339,1016,'block_0_fields',''),(14340,1016,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(14341,1016,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(14342,1016,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpement-de-notre-activite-bitume-en-afrique'),(14343,1016,'_wp_old_slug','guyane-premiere-centrale-electrique-multi-megawatts-a-hydrogene-au-monde'),(14344,1016,'_yoast_wpseo_title','NIGERIA: Rehabilitation of school buildings in Abudja'),(14345,1016,'_yoast_wpseo_metadesc','The latest project carried out by Ringardas with the financial support of the Rubis Group.'),(14346,1016,'block_1_fields_text','<strong>Après l\'acquisition de 24,99 % du capital de KenolKobil Plc, le Groupe Rubis annonce ce jour son intention de lancer une offre publique d\'achat sur le capital restant, conformément au règlement applicable à la Bourse de Nairobi, au Kenyan Capital Markets Act ainsi que toutes autres lois et règlements applicables.</strong>\r\n\r\nKenolKobil, leader de la distribution de produits pétroliers au Kenya, est également implanté au Burundi, Éthiopie, Ouganda, Rwanda et Zambie avec un volume global en distribution finale de 1,3million de m3 en 2017.\r\n\r\nKenolKobil regroupe l\'ensemble des activités de distribution de produits pétroliers : réseaux (350 stations-service), carburants aviation, GPL, lubrifiants, bitume, commercial et industriel, avec des accès sécurisés aux oléoducs et son maillage de 10 terminaux.\r\n\r\nLe secteur de la distribution de produits pétroliers en Afrique de l\'Est bénéficie d\'une demande en croissance régulière, tirée par le développement démographique, l\'urbanisation et les investissements dans les infrastructures routières. Avec un bassin de population supérieur à 200 millions d\'habitants, KenolKobil offre de solides perspectives de développement.\r\n\r\nDepuis 2013, KenolKobil enregistre une croissance régulière de ses volumes et de ses résultats avec un RBE normalisé de 50 millions d\'USD généré en 2017 et présente une structure financière solide.\r\n\r\nÀ 23 KES (Kenyan Shillings) par action, l\'offre de Rubis valorise KenolKobil à 353 millions d\'USD (pour 100 %), financés par les moyens propres du Groupe avec un effet relutif immédiat.\r\n\r\nLe lancement définitif de l\'offre publique est soumis à l\'approbation des autorités régionales et nationales de la concurrence et de toute autre autorité compétente.\r\n\r\n<a href=\"https://rubiskenya.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">KenolKobil</a> correspond parfaitement aux objectifs et critères d\'investissement du Groupe Rubis et viendra idéalement compléter la position de RUBIS ENERGIE en Afrique, dans un secteur particulièrement prometteur où le Groupe entend apporter une nouvelle impulsion.\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a href=\"https://www.rubisenergie.com/uploads/noi-final-artwork-24102018.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Annonce publique : OPA</a></p>\r\n<p class=\"rteright\"><a class=\"target-blank\" href=\"https://rubis.fr/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Groupe Rubis</a></p>'),(14347,1016,'_block_1_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(14348,1016,'_yoast_wpseo_primary_category','138'),(14349,1016,'_thumbnail_id','945'),(14350,1016,'post_imgs',''),(14351,1016,'_post_imgs','field_614dc88d40bbc'),(14352,1016,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Liberia'),(14353,1016,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','28'),(14355,1016,'_dp_original','944'),(14356,1016,'_edit_lock','1635791482:2'),(14357,1016,'_edit_last','2'),(14359,1016,'_wp_old_date','2021-11-01'),(14361,1016,'_wp_old_slug','nigeria-rehabilitation-of-school-buildings-in-abudja'),(14363,1015,'_wp_old_date','2021-10-15'),(14365,1016,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-01'),(14367,864,'_wp_old_slug','caraibes-le-morbihan-dernier-ne-de-la-flotte-rubis'),(14370,751,'_wp_old_slug','madagascar-team-bulding-chez-galana'),(14372,944,'_wp_old_slug','nigeria-refection-de-batiments-scolaires-a-abudja'),(14377,670,'_yoast_wpseo_focuskw','Plastic Odyssey'),(14378,670,'_yoast_wpseo_linkdex','38'),(14380,672,'_y