3,'header_page_img','1652'),(19094,1653,'_header_page_img','field_60dad753a56c0'),(19095,1653,'header_page',''),(19096,1653,'_header_page','field_60dad72fa56bc'),(19097,1653,'_yoast_wpseo_content_score','90'),(19098,1653,'_yoast_wpseo_estimated-reading-time-minutes','1'),(19099,1653,'_wp_old_date','2021-07-06'),(19100,1653,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-15'),(19101,1653,'_wp_old_date','2021-09-17'),(19102,1653,'_wp_old_date','2021-10-08'),(19103,1653,'_wp_old_date','2021-10-21'),(19104,1653,'_wp_old_date','2022-05-23'),(19105,1653,'_wp_old_date','2022-04-19'),(19106,1653,'_wp_old_date','2022-10-28'),(19107,1653,'block_0_fields_text','<span style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; color: black;\">October 2022\r\n</span>\r\n<div id=\"Tdet\">\r\n\r\nOn 12 October 2022, <strong>Maritec Tanker Management</strong> proudly took delivery of a new vessel, the <strong>DEMERARA</strong>, 9,150 DWT IMO II, for <strong>Rubis Eastern Caribbean</strong> (REC).\r\n\r\nThe DEMERARA is a sister ship to the <strong>MORBIHAN</strong>, which was commissioned a year ago. She will also be positioned in the Caribbean to reinforce the Group\'s logistics and supplies.\r\n\r\nAt the end of September, a new bitumen tanker, the <strong>BITU RIVER</strong>, left the shipyards for West Africa and by the end of October, the bitumen tanker <strong>VIVEKA</strong> will be withdrawn from the fleet for demolition at a ship recycling yard in Bangladesh. The VIVEKA was built in 1994 and was purchased by the Group in 2014. Over the past 8 years she has mainly sailed in West Africa to supply our bitumen terminals in Nigeria and Togo.\r\n\r\nWith these changes in the Rubis Energie fleet, the number of vessels managed by Maritec Tanker Management is now 8.\r\n\r\n</div>'),(19108,1653,'_block_0_fields_text','field_5d318356707db'),(19109,1653,'block_0_fields',''),(19110,1653,'_block_0_fields','field_5d31c477d5643'),(19111,1653,'_wp_old_slug','rubis-energie-en-afrique-de-lest-3'),(19112,1653,'_wp_old_slug','gabon-nouveau-developpe